# NOTE: E057 (IncludePathNotAllowed) requires --allow-path configuration which restricts
# file includes to specific directory roots. Without --allow-path, all paths are allowed.
# With --allow-path set, attempts to include files outside the allowed roots trigger E057.
# The current corpus test infrastructure does not support passing --allow-path configuration.
# This error path is exercised via CLI integration tests in main.rs.
#
# The existing tests/corpus/eval/errors/include_path_not_allowed.llt-eval actually tests
# E042 (IncludeForbidden via # no_fs directive), not E057.
#
# To enable corpus testing of E057, we would need:
# 1. A directive like `# allow_path /some/root` in split_test_file()
# 2. Extension of eval_source_with_config() to accept allow_path parameter
# 3. A test fixture directory structure to test path traversal restrictions
#
# This file exists as documentation of the gap and will be updated when infrastructure supports it.
